From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:36:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Quests: in-world NPC talk UX, anonymous cast skins, living
 cast
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Placed-NPC overhaul for the Aetherion harbour/tutorial/world cast.

- Talk UX: TextDisplay speech bubbles (typewriter + per-NPC voice) and
  reply chips (Interaction hitboxes: look+click, scroll+click, chat
  mirror) with a quest card. Quest accept/decline/gates run through the
  existing DialogManager handlers; chest Quest Offer stays behind
  "Details…", for /npctalk classic, QA bots and every fallback.
- Skins: removed the auto-assigned famous-creator Mojang skins. 39
  original cast skins (docs/npc/skins/paint_skins.py) signed through
  FancyNpcs' MineSkin upload and cached in skins-signed.yml; unsigned
  NPCs keep leather on a default body. Editor presets anonymised.
- Dialogue: rewritten lines for the placed set with {player} tokens,
  return-visit intros, stage-aware completed lines, reactions, small-
  talk topics, in-world Ledger help desk.
- Life: LivingNpcLife work beats, glances, tiny ground-checked patrols,
  gestures/emotes; LivingNpcAtmosphere greet-by-name, idle barks, banter.
- NpcMemory (npc-memory.yml), /npctalk, /questnpc extras (3 idea NPCs).
- DE overlay: factual fixes (no Dock Pass, "Klick", Harrow in German).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
